course: dictionary
lesson: 14797
title: Punctuality
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Punctuality means being on time, not late. A punctual person arrives when they should, and a punctual bus or train arrives when its timetable says it will. Punctuality is a noun, so it names a quality, as in «her punctuality».
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mia was never late for school, and her punctuality made the teachers smile.» The words «never late» tell you that punctuality is about arriving on time. Try the swap: «her being on time made the teachers smile» still makes sense, so punctuality means being on time.
explain: Punctuality is something people praise. «The school report praised Sam for his punctuality and good attendance.» A report only praises good things, so punctuality is a good quality to have. In maths, times such as «the bus leaves at 8:15» and «it arrives at 8:40» help you check how punctual a bus was.
fact: Punctuality means being on time, not late.
fact: Punctuality is a noun: you can say «good punctuality» or «her punctuality».
fact: «Punctual» is the matching adjective: «Mia is punctual» means Mia is on time.
fact: Trains and buses are judged by their punctuality: how often they arrive on time.
fact: In time problems, punctuality is about start and arrival times: if a lesson starts at 9:00 and you walk in at 9:00, you are punctual.
exercise: «Mia was never late, and her punctuality made the teachers smile.» What does punctuality mean? | Being very loud in class | Being tired after lunch | *Being on time | Being good at drawing
exercise: «The train had good punctuality, arriving at 10:15 every single day.» What does good punctuality mean here? | Arriving late every day | Never leaving the station | Sleeping on the train | *Arriving on time, every day
exercise: A lesson starts at 9:00. Ella walks in at 9:00 exactly. What does this show? | Lateness | Sadness | *Punctuality | Talking loudly
test: «The school report praised Sam for his punctuality.» Which is the opposite of being punctual? | Being quiet | Being kind | Being on time | *Being late
test: A bus leaves at 8:00 and arrives at 8:05. Was it punctual? | Yes, it was early | Yes, exactly on time | Not enough information to know | *No, it was five minutes late
exam: Which sentence shows punctuality? | The bus was muddy and slow | Mia lost her bag on the way | Tom forgot his lunch again | *The bus always arrived at 8:00 on the dot
